            "heading": "Wear Your Life Jacket",
            "body": "From 1 July 2026, everyone on the exposed deck of a fishing vessel must wear a life jacket, regardless of weather warnings or crew size. The captain faces fines of KRW 900,000 (1st offence), 1.5 million (2nd), and up to 3 million (3rd or more) — and the rule applies equally to foreign crew. According to KOMSA, about 81% of those who died or went missing at sea over the last five years were not wearing one; the Coast Guard estimates survival rises to about 78% when a jacket is worn. In cold water you have roughly 1 minute of cold shock, 10 minutes of useful movement, and 1 hour before losing consciousness (the 1-10-1 principle) — putting a jacket on after falling in is already too late. Fasten the buckle firmly and tighten it against your body."
