            "heading": "Responding to Bad Weather",
            "body": "A wind-wave advisory (풍랑주의보) is issued when average wind speed exceeds 14 m/s for 3+ hours or waves are expected above 3 m. Smaller fishing vessels are barred from departing during an advisory, and violations can lead to suspension or cancellation of the fishing permit. Check marine weather before every departure, follow the captain's and Coast Guard's decisions, and if a warning catches you at sea: put on your life jacket, secure loose gear, reduce speed, and keep the bow into the waves."
