            "heading": "Fire Prevention and Response",
            "body": "Engine room fires (fuel or lube oil reaching hot surfaces) and galley fires account for most vessel fires. Inspect piping regularly, repair leaks immediately, and never overload circuits. If fire breaks out, raise the alarm and inform the captain first. Never use water on galley or oil fires — smother the fire or use the correct extinguisher."
